{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "description": "Operational dashboard for the memory-extraction subsystem (V2.2 P2.2). Every panel answers one operational question: A working, B slower, C failures rising, D queue filling, E workers saturated, F Redis coordination, G provider/model, H memories created. Bounded-label metrics only; no user/session/message/run IDs, no conversation content.",
  "editable": false,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "liveNow": false,
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "owngpt_prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Operational trust gating every other panel: is the app being scraped (up=1) and is extraction enabled by configuration (info=1)? If either is missing, read the other panels with suspicion.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": { "mode": "thresholds" },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "red", "value": null },
              { "color": "green", "value": 1 }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "up{job=\"owngpt-web\"}",
          "legendFormat": "app up",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "owngpt_memory_extraction_info{enabled=\"1\"}",
          "legendFormat": "extraction enabled",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "System health",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "owngpt_prometheus"
      },
      "description": "A. Is extraction working? Scheduled attempts land per user message; completed runs reach a terminal decision. Gaps or divergence between the two signal scheduling or worker problems.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "color": { "mode": "palette-classic" }, "custom": { "fillOpacity": 10, "lineWidth": 1, "showPoints": "never" }, "unit": "reqps" },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 6, "y": 0 },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_scheduled_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "scheduled",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_completed_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "completed",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Extraction throughput",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "owngpt_prometheus"
      },
      "description": "B. Is extraction getting slower? End-to-end attempt duration (claim to terminal decision) at p50/p90/p95. Trend, not absolute value, is the question here.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "color": { "mode": "palette-classic" }, "custom": { "fillOpacity": 0, "lineWidth": 2, "showPoints": "never" }, "unit": "s" },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 4 },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.90, sum by (le) (rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p90",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Extraction duration p50/p90/p95",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "owngpt_prometheus"
      },
      "description": "C. Are failures increasing? Failure rate by bounded reason taxonomy. A new reason appearing or any sustained rate is actionable (check ExtractionFailureRateHigh).",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "color": { "mode": "palette-classic" }, "custom": { "fillOpacity": 30, "lineWidth": 1, "showPoints": "never" }, "unit": "reqps" },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 6, "y": 4 },
      "id": 4,
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_failed_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Extraction failures by reason",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "owngpt_prometheus"
      },
      "description": "E. Workers saturated? Inflight is owned exclusively by the executor; a flat, sustained plateau at the configured max concurrency (while the queue grows) is saturation. The queue panel below confirms it.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "color": { "mode": "palette-classic" }, "custom": { "fillOpacity": 10, "lineWidth": 2, "showPoints": "never" }, "unit": "short" },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 11 },
      "id": 5,
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "owngpt_memory_extraction_inflight",
          "legendFormat": "inflight",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Inflight extractions (workers busy)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "owngpt_prometheus"
      },
      "description": "D. Is the queue filling? Depth approaching capacity (ExtractionQueueBacklog fires at 90%) means scheduling outpaces the worker pool.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "color": { "mode": "palette-classic" }, "custom": { "fillOpacity": 10, "lineWidth": 1, "showPoints": "never" }, "unit": "short" },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 6, "y": 11 },
      "id": 6,
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "owngpt_memory_extraction_queue_depth",
          "legendFormat": "queue depth",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "owngpt_memory_extraction_queue_capacity",
          "legendFormat": "queue capacity",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Extraction queue depth vs capacity",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "owngpt_prometheus"
      },
      "description": "F. Is Redis coordination degrading? Claims granted vs denied, and the fail-open fallback rate per operation. Any sustained fallback is abnormal in the compose deployment.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "color": { "mode": "palette-classic" }, "custom": { "fillOpacity": 10, "lineWidth": 1, "showPoints": "never" }, "unit": "reqps" },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 18 },
      "id": 7,
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_redis_claim_success_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "claims granted",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_redis_claim_conflict_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "claims denied",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (operation) (rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_redis_fallback_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "fallback {{operation}}",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Redis coordination",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "owngpt_prometheus"
      },
      "description": "G. Which provider/model is in use? Calls and errors per bounded provider-model pair; token consumption per kind where the provider reports it. Model label is config-allowlisted (plus 'other'), never free-form.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "color": { "mode": "palette-classic" }, "custom": { "fillOpacity": 10, "lineWidth": 1, "showPoints": "never" }, "unit": "reqps" },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 6, "y": 18 },
      "id": 8,
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (provider, model) (rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_llm_calls_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "calls {{provider}}/{{model}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (provider, model) (rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_llm_errors_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "errors {{provider}}/{{model}}",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (kind) (rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_llm_tokens_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "tokens {{kind}}",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "title": "LLM calls, errors, tokens by provider/model",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "owngpt_prometheus"
      },
      "description": "H. Are memories actually being created? Created by status, plus deduplicated, conflict-pending and superseded outcomes. This is the final evidence that storage follows from extraction.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "color": { "mode": "palette-classic" }, "custom": { "fillOpacity": 10, "lineWidth": 1, "showPoints": "never" }, "unit": "reqps" },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 25 },
      "id": 9,
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (status) (rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_memory_created_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "created {{status}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_memory_deduplicated_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "deduplicated",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_memory_conflict_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "conflict-pending",
          "refId": "C"
        },
        {
          "expr": "rate(owngpt_memory_extraction_memory_superseded_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "superseded",
          "refId": "D"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Memories created and outcome counters",
      "type": "timeseries"
    }
  ],
  "refresh": "30s",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "tags": ["owngpt", "memory-extraction", "v2.2-p2.2"],
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timepicker": {
    "refresh_intervals": ["5s", "10s", "30s", "1m", "5m"]
  },
  "timezone": "browser",
  "title": "OwnGPT Memory Extraction",
  "uid": "owngpt-extraction",
  "version": 1,
  "weekStart": ""
}